The Kaftian population included a small number of escapees who crossed the sea from [[Lacashe]], where slavery remained legal. The trickle was not large enough to shift the demographic balance but was noticeable in coastal communities, particularly in [[Waribá]] and [[Barikú]].

=== Urbanisation ===

Urbanisation continued the slow upward trend established in the previous century. The urban share of the population rose from approximately 30% in 1824 to approximately 33% by 1853. The three principal urban centres grew modestly:

